  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nNear persistent conditions extend into Thursday with high temps 10\nto 15 degrees above normal. Attention will become the tropical\nremnants and associated mid level wave lifting into west TX on\nFriday. Widespread rains will initially remain west of the local \narea through much of Friday before expanding east across the \nforecast area Friday night into Saturday. Bulk of guidance keeps \nrainfall amounts rather light during this time frame but any \namounts will be welcome in the ongoing drought conditions. \nInstability is likely to remain low with the wave passage so any \ncoverage of thunderstorms will remain low with minimal impact to \noutdoor events on Saturday. Precip timing across the forecast \narea remains similar with the latest guidance and favors rains \nending from west to east mid Saturday afternoon through late \nSaturday evening. \n\nA brief dry period is forecast for Sunday before influence from a\npotentially  stronger storm system returns precip chances to the \nregion Monday. The early week storm system has high uncertainty at\nthis time range but early trends in guidance have been for a \nwidespread influence across the central CONUS. The forecast will \nreflect this by maintaining fairly high precip chances for early \nnext week.",
